From 160a77d4c508eda7bc8719c0c2701bb3a03a5943 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abito <33889084+abitocodes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:10:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix reversed survey options, HEP above 1 and reversed
 text maps

- input.html: fill optionCodeNumbersByField so sleep hours, procedure
  complexity, yellow dust and floor friction send the code whose value
  matches its meaning (2 = worst). The table was empty, so these four
  items were sent reversed. The direction is confirmed by the Korail
  worker survey (e.g. under 6 h of sleep is rated worse than 8 h+).
- result.html, detail_result.html: when the saturation correction is
  used, combine diagnosis and execution HEP as 1-(1-d)(1-e) instead of
  adding them, so the final HEP stays <= 1 (it reached ~2 before).
- config/mappings.py: jargon_need_map and info_uncertainty_map had 0 and
  2 swapped (used by the CNN path).
- tests: regression test that the final HEP stays <= 1 with every PSF
  at its worst level (fails on the previous code with 1.99999).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
